These  utilities  are user tools to manipulate the named extended
attributes on files and directories.  The argument should be  the
namespace  of the attribute to retrieve: legal values are and For
all operations except the namespace argument may  be  omitted  if
the  attribute  name is namespace prefixed, like in In that later
case, the namespace  prefix  obviously  selects  namespace.   and
namespace  prefixes select the namespace.  The argument should be
the name of the attribute, the name of the target file or  direc‐
tory,  a string to store in the attribute.  The following options
are available: (Force.)  Ignore errors  on  individual  filenames
and  continue with the remaining arguments.  (No follow.)  If the
file is a symbolic link, perform the operation on the link itself
rather than the file that the  link  points  to.   (Input  file.)
